Shafaq News- Erbil Iraq will bring armed factions&rsquo; weapons under state control and prevent activities outside state authority by June 30, 2027, Sabah al-Numan, spokesman for the commander-in-ch
Speaking at a panel during the Middle East Research Institute (MERI) Forum 2026 in Erbil, titled &ldquo;After the Global Coalition: Iraq, the Kurdistan Region and the New Regional Balance,&rdquo; al-Numan added that the withdrawal of the US-led Coalition &ldquo;had removed all pretexts for refusing to place weapons under state control and unify security decision-making.&rdquo;
He said that armed factions had pledged to honor a &ldquo;goodwill initiative&rdquo; and comply with a 90-day deadline announced by the government to halt any activities targeting a neighboring country. &ldquo;All of Iraq&rsquo;s borders are now fully secured, and no entity operating outside the law can threaten a neighboring country.&rdquo;
